{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-post-template-tsx","path":"/posts/why-you-need-a-personal-mission-statement/","result":{"data":{"markdownRemark":{"id":"dc1ae6d9-e4d0-53c1-b044-6d907afb20b8","html":"<p>Most of us stay busy without asking why. Stephen Covey calls this out in Habit 2 of <em>The 7 Habits of Highly Effective People</em>: Begin with the End in Mind. His answer to it is a personal mission statement.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-it-is\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#what-it-is\" aria-label=\"what it is permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>What It Is</h2>\n<p>A personal mission statement is a written declaration of your core values, your purpose, and the kind of person you’ve decided to be. Not a goal list. Not a vision board. Think of it as a personal constitution — the document you return to when a hard decision lands, or when life knocks you sideways and you need to find your footing again.</p>\n<p>It doesn’t ask what you want to achieve. It asks who you want to become.</p>\n<p>Two very different questions.</p>\n<h2 id=\"why-it-matters\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#why-it-matters\" aria-label=\"why it matters permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>Why It Matters</h2>\n<p>Without a defined center, most people default to one of two modes: reacting to whatever feels urgent, or performing for whoever is watching.</p>\n<p>Covey puts it plainly:</p>\n<figure>\n\t<blockquote>\n\t\t<p>It's incredibly easy to get caught up in an activity trap, in the busyness of life, to work harder and harder at climbing the ladder of success only to discover it's leaning against the wrong wall.</p>\n\t\t<footer>\n\t\t\t<cite>— Stephen Covey, The 7 Habits of Highly Effective People</cite>\n\t\t</footer>\n\t</blockquote>\n</figure>\n<p>A mission statement gives you a compass — not just a map. Maps tell you how to get somewhere; a compass tells you which direction actually matters to you.</p>\n<h2 id=\"how-to-write-one\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#how-to-write-one\" aria-label=\"how to write one permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>How to Write One</h2>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 960px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/911f772a95ad98fea22f912f285074a7/809bc/image1.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 22.083333333333332%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <picture>\n          <source\n              srcset=\"/static/911f772a95ad98fea22f912f285074a7/8ac56/image1.webp 240w,\n/static/911f772a95ad98fea22f912f285074a7/d3be9/image1.webp 480w,\n/static/911f772a95ad98fea22f912f285074a7/e46b2/image1.webp 960w,\n/static/911f772a95ad98fea22f912f285074a7/f992d/image1.webp 1440w,\n/static/911f772a95ad98fea22f912f285074a7/882b9/image1.webp 1920w,\n/static/911f772a95ad98fea22f912f285074a7/81ab8/image1.webp 2612w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"\n              type=\"image/webp\"\n            />\n          <source\n            srcset=\"/static/911f772a95ad98fea22f912f285074a7/8ff5a/image1.png 240w,\n/static/911f772a95ad98fea22f912f285074a7/e85cb/image1.png 480w,\n/static/911f772a95ad98fea22f912f285074a7/d9199/image1.png 960w,\n/static/911f772a95ad98fea22f912f285074a7/07a9c/image1.png 1440w,\n/static/911f772a95ad98fea22f912f285074a7/29114/image1.png 1920w,\n/static/911f772a95ad98fea22f912f285074a7/809bc/image1.png 2612w\"\n            sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"\n            type=\"image/png\"\n          />\n          <img\n            class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n            src=\"/static/911f772a95ad98fea22f912f285074a7/d9199/image1.png\"\n            alt=\"Steps on how to write a personal mission statement\"\n            title=\"\"\n            loading=\"lazy\"\n            decoding=\"async\"\n            style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n          />\n        </picture>\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>Covey suggests starting with a thought experiment: imagine your own funeral. What would you want people to say about you — as a partner, a colleague, a friend? The life you’d want eulogized is the life your mission statement should point toward.</p>\n<p>There’s no perfect format. Some are a single sentence. Others are structured by life domain — family, work, health, personal growth. What matters is that it reflects you — not a polished version of who you think you should be.</p>\n<h2 id=\"a-real-example\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#a-real-example\" aria-label=\"a real example permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>A Real Example</h2>\n<p>Here is my personal mission statement — seven commitments, each specific and actionable.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://cedricsarigumba.notion.site/Personal-Mission-Statements-13478639b44d8017826ac2f162ead615\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Read it here →</a></p>","timeToRead":1,"fields":{"slug":"/posts/2026-03-08---personal-mission-statement//posts/why-you-need-a-personal-mission-statement","tagSlugs":["/tag/personal-development/","/tag/7-habits/","/tag/stephen-covey/","/tag/mission-statement/"]},"frontmatter":{"date":"2026-03-08T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["Personal Development","7 Habits","Stephen Covey","Mission Statement"],"title":"Why You Need a Personal Mission Statement","description":"Are You Going Somewhere, or Just Busy?","socialImage":"./image.jpg"}}},"pageContext":{"slug":"/posts/2026-03-08---personal-mission-statement//posts/why-you-need-a-personal-mission-statement"}},"staticQueryHashes":["4208939363"],"slicesMap":{}}